# Strict TypeScript & Zod — production contract

`any` is a product defect. This kit compiles with `strict`, `noImplicitAny`,
`strictNullChecks`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `useUnknownInCatchVariables`.
ESLint errors on `TSAnyKeyword`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-nocheck`, and double
assertions (`as unknown as T`).

## Types

- Prefer `type` aliases for objects that must satisfy
  `Record<string, unknown>` (Supabase `Database` rows). Interfaces lack
  implicit index signatures.
- Domain types live in `types/` (`database.ts`, `auth.ts`, `billing.ts`,
  `rbac.ts`, `agent.ts`). Do not declare throwaway shapes in UI files.
- Catch bindings are `unknown`. Run them through
  `isolateUnknownError(error, "stable_code")` before any UI or JSON alert.
- JSON.parse returns `any` in TypeScript. Always wrap with
  `parseJsonUnknown()` so the value is `unknown`, then Zod-parse.
- Exhaustive `switch` on discriminated unions. Use `never` in the default
  branch when the union is closed; unknown Stripe/Lemon event types may
  `return` instead of throwing.
- Do not use non-null assertions (`!`). Narrow or return early.
- Insert/Update types for tables must be `Pick` / `Partial` of the Row type
  so a made-up column fails the build (`AssertKeysSubset`).

## Zod

- Zod 4 is the parser (`zod` ^4). Do not add Zod 3 APIs (`ZodError.errors`
  shape differs).
- Every trust boundary has a schema in `lib/security/api-schemas.ts` or
  `lib/auth/schemas.ts`:
  - query strings (OAuth `next` must match `^\/(?!\/)[A-Za-z0-9/_-]*$`)
  - JSON bodies (`emptyJsonBodySchema` is `.strict()` — extra keys are 400)
  - webhook envelopes (after HMAC, never before)
  - env (`lib/security/env-schema.ts`)
- `safeParse` at the edge. Do not `parse()` in a Route Handler unless you
  catch and map to a named 400.
- Env placeholders containing `YOUR_` are rejected. Do not “fix” that refine.
- Infer types with `z.infer<typeof schema>`. Keep a compile-time
  `AssertEqual<z.infer<typeof rowSchema>, Row>` for SQL-shaped objects.

## Errors

- Named machine codes in JSON: `{ error: "invalid_signature" }`.
- HTTP mapping: 400 inspect/HMAC/Zod, 401 no user, 403 role, 409 missing
  Stripe customer, 500 after a verified event failed to apply.
- Never send stack traces, raw webhook bodies, or secrets to the client.
